    "body": "Literal selection retained exact queried-entity cues but lacked a learned code for a relevant query/cue match, so reordered facts could make it copy the other entity's value. Continue the existing signed-H4 literal router with all 52 observed missing codes, retaining all 567 old codes and the fixed dictionary/feature law. An explicit witness reconstructs the complete 433e3807 parent. Computed roles, numeric admission, source/NoRead and all other parameters remain fixed; no new serving head or state is added.\n\nRetain `e1ef0a5d` at bounded literal selection scope. Complete construction improves 571/631 → 630/631 with 59 gains and no lost correct answer; disabling refinement restores all 631 parent texts/stops. Open answers improve 4/8 → 8/8. Fresh changed-name/value/place/order answers improve 8/16 → 16/16 versus 8/16 matched equality. Both fits finish the configured schedule. All prior output/write/session preservation passes. The previous admission set improves 8/12 → 10/12; its two supported-location abstentions remain. The lone construction error is also a supported-location abstention. These are bounded authored-world results, not general language or frontier capability.\n\nValidation: offline release example, public CLI and final test target compile; actual-artifact parent/mutation, disabled control, causal writes, mismatched observation, checkpoint and zero-allocation checks pass. All 32 repaired swapped-name Rust programs execute their original assertions. The rebuilt public CLI emits the correct reordered fresh value. Exact native-kernel source, formatting, architecture-policy and claim-wording checks pass. An earlier mistyped source-test filter selected zero tests and is recorded as unrun evidence; the corrected exact test passes. Eighteen warm predict/observe samples measure 0.120 ms median and 0.216 ms maximum, excluding loading/encoding/ingestion/checkpoints. No end-to-end, matched-speedup or energy claim. Full release/Clippy/WASM were not run; protected status names acknowledge compatibility only.\n\nModel work 242.829 s; engineering 637.694 s. Existing cumulative model use is 4011.935/4170 s, leaving 158.065 s. Sampled known storage growth is 298,889,216 bytes within the 384 MiB projection; peak sampled model-child RSS is 986,988,544 bytes. No budget extension, external compute or deletion. The result and full evidence are in `docs/native_geometric_literal_binding_1139.md` and its JSON receipt. Current-state/README/research/plan now point next to order-sensitive supported-source/NoRead selection while preserving this binding.\n\nRefs #1139, #1140, #973. Broader capability issues remain open.\n",
